## Frontend Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|---|---|
| Framework | Vanilla TypeScript (Vite) |
| Bundler | Vite |
| Tauri API | `@tauri-apps/api` v2 |
| Styling | CSS Modules / Tailwind CSS |

### Frontend ↔ Rust IPC

- Frontend calls Rust via `invoke('command_name', { ...args })`.
- Rust emits events to frontend via `app.emit('event_name', payload)`.
- Never use `window.__TAURI__` directly — always use the typed `@tauri-apps/api` wrappers.
{{/if}}

## MCP Integration (if active)

If `mcp-server.json` is present in the project root, Kiro can read MCP tools.
MCP tools are listed in `context/mcp-tools.md`. Do not install new MCP tools without updating that file.

## Dependencies: Never Add Without Approval

- No new Cargo dependencies not listed in the approved manifest (`Cargo.toml` workspace members).
- No new npm packages not listed in the approved frontend toolkit.
- For Tauri plugins, propose the addition in `openspec/changes/` first.
- Do not upgrade Tauri major versions without an architecture proposal.

## Workspace Layout

```
Cargo.toml               — Workspace root
crates/
  {{project.rust.cratePrefix}}-domain/        — Pure domain logic (no I/O)
  {{project.rust.cratePrefix}}-application/   — Use cases, commands, queries
  {{project.rust.cratePrefix}}-infrastructure/ — SQLite, file system, OS
  {{project.rust.cratePrefix}}-desktop/       — Tauri commands, app entry point
{{#if project.features.frontend}}
frontend/                — Vite TypeScript frontend
  src/                   — TypeScript source
  index.html
{{/if}}
```
